{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2020-12-03 14:35:00', 'title': 'PG&E RECEIVES STATE APPROVAL FOR INVESTMENTS AIMED AT IMPROVING SAFETY, REDUCING WILDFIRE RISK AND BUILDING A STRONGER ENERGY SYSTEM FOR THE FUTURE', 'text': "SAN FRANCISCO--(BUSINESS WIRE)--TODAY, THE CALIFORNIA PUBLIC UTILITIES COMMISSION (CPUC) APPROVED MOST ASPECTS OF A MULTI-PARTY SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT BETWEEN PACIFIC GAS AND ELECTRIC COMPANY (PG&E OR THE UTILITY) AND CUSTOMER ADVOCACY, LABOR AND SAFETY GROUPS THAT RESOLVED PG&E'S 2020-2022 GENERAL RATE CASE (GRC), WHICH INCLUDES THE UTILITY'S ONGOING EFFORTS TO REDUCE WILDFIRE RISK AND TO CONTINUE DELIVERING SAFE AND RELIABLE SERVICE TO CUSTOMERS. THE GRC DECISION ENABLES NECESSARY INVES"}